Hell's Bells! That sounds rather extinctionistic. If you cast "create
monster" a lot, did you recover power by invoking your quest artefact,
or did you wish for the Eye of the Aethiopica?

 I decided to try my hand at a combat
> class.  My Knight died on the Quest (having never found any sort of bag or
> any special armor whatsoever)

Knights have a knack of having particularly bad luck with the RNG.
They do start with bad Dx and To very often, but that shouldn't be
that much of a disadvantage - archeologists are much worse off.

> Anyway... I've gotten down to the castle, and completed the quest.
> Current inventory / stats look something like this:

> Stats - 800 HP, 33 PW (ack!), -55 AC, XL 20, crowned, disintegration
> resistant, teleport/control, all stats maxed except INT=11, CHA=11

I don't know the source part for it, but it seems that dwarfs get
particularly bad Pw ratings. If you gained a lot of Wisdom recently,
you _could_ get yourself drained several levels (but not down to
zero!), then recover them; this has a good chance of putting you on a
somewhat more sound footing - but obviously it's a pretty strange
thing to do.

> I'm currently wishless - genoless - polyselfless - polypileless (I did
> make a tin opener testing potions though.)

Of course, the conduct is gone nonetheless. I checked and it seems
that even "Nothing seems to happen." increases your "items
polymorphed" counter, even though the item "polymorphed" into yet
another sample of what it was before. The potion can be identified by
hitting a monster with it, but that is rather hazardous, and not at
all guaranteed to work.

> Here are some of the options I've thought of:
> - reverse geno silver dragons for scales, chug a couple !oGEnergy and get
> rid of the shield, so I can cast magic missile reliably and effectively
> - go kill a priest for a robe, and polypile for an "oReflection so I can
> get rid of the shield and cast magic missile...

I think the latter is more likely to work for you; valkyries are
_very_ bad at casting spells, and i think that their minimum fail
rates without a robe are significantly above 0%. You'll still want a
lot more Pw if you want to use spells. The final "explosion" of magic
traps fills up your Pw and adds to the max, btw. Nothing for the faint
of heart, of course (can create mind flayers!).

[still mind flayers]
> What are some other options? 

Greasing your helmet provides a layer (ahem) of safety. Mind flayers
respect Elbereth, if you don't find that too cheap. Conflict or a
powerful pet (preferably a purple worm or something that wears a
helmet) have potential for diverting the *flayer's attacks to someone
else. There's also cockatrice eggs, and (for novelty value) you could
polymorph into something without a head or into a cockatrice.

> What should I do to give this character good
> chances of surviving? 

Just don't perform any approved Really Stupid Moves [tm]. In your
current shape, you're pretty much unkaputtbar[1] .

> Is it worth trying to keep conducts, or should I
> just geno at will?

If you're really adverse to losing your memories, genocide would be
the easiest option; if you think you ought to bravely tackle mind
flayers, you can just as well do this in another game.

[1] silly german neologism meaning "impossible to kaputt", and no,
"kaputt" isn't a verb in german, either

